// bubbler profile: keepassxc
//
// No `network`: KeePassXC needs none to open a database. firejail's
// profile agrees and goes further with `net none`. The flathub manifest
// grants `--share=network` for favicon download alone; add `network`
// yourself if you use that feature, and understand that it is your
// password database's process reaching the internet.
//
// No `own "org.freedesktop.secrets"`. That rule, added to the `dbus`
// block below, makes this sandbox the Secret Service for the whole
// session: every application that stores a password through libsecret
// stores it here. It is an outward grant rather than a confinement (see
// the README), and first owner wins, so a host keyring already holding
// the name only makes the request fail. Add it if you mean to replace
// that keyring:
//     own "org.freedesktop.secrets"
//
// No `hidraw`, and it would not help: KeePassXC reaches a YubiKey
// through libusb (/dev/bus/usb plus /sys/bus/usb) and a smart card
// through pcsclite — the binary links both libraries and holds no
// hidraw string at all. bubbler has no raw-USB grant yet, so
// challenge-response unlocking does not work from this sandbox; see
// "Known gaps".
//
// Browser integration does not work from here yet: the proxy socket is
// inside the sandbox and the browser is outside it. See "Known gaps".
//
// The database lives in the private home unless you share the directory
// holding it; `home-share "Documents" mode=rw` is a starting point, and
// a database on another disk is named explicitly, e.g.
//     path-share "/kioxia/keepass" mode=rw
wayland
dbus {
    own "org.keepassxc.KeePassXC.*"
    talk "org.freedesktop.ScreenSaver"
}
portals
notify
tray
home-share "Documents" mode=rw
command "keepassxc"
